---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CompositionNav from '../../components/CompositionNav.astro';
import { artifacts, outcomes } from '../../data/composition';

const majorArtifacts = artifacts.slice(0, 3);
---

<Layout
	title="Composition Research Portfolio | EPPPE.NET"
	description="Carmine Iacona’s final ENC 1102 ePortfolio, including six outcome reflections, three Gordon Rule assignments, research process work, and the completed interview study."
>
	<header class="composition-hero">
		<div class="shell composition-hero__inner">
			<div class="composition-hero__copy">
				<p class="eyebrow">ENC 1102 · Summer 2026</p>
				<h1>Writing in<br /><em>class group chats.</em></h1>
				<p class="composition-hero__deck">
					My ENC 1102 research project looks at how students use unofficial class group chats to ask questions, clarify assignments, and support one another.
				</p>
				<div class="composition-hero__meta">
					<span>Carmine Iacona</span>
					<span>Dr. Rebecca Watkins</span>
					<span>Composition II</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<aside class="research-card">
				<p class="research-card__label">Semester research question</p>
				<p class="research-card__question">
					How do college students use student-run class group chats to clarify course expectations and support one another outside official classroom spaces?
				</p>
				<div class="research-card__stats">
					<div><strong>03</strong><span>Gordon Rule artifacts</span></div>
					<div><strong>06</strong><span>Course outcomes</span></div>
					<div><strong>11</strong><span>Selected artifacts</span></div>
					<div><strong>05</strong><span>Interviews</span></div>
				</div>
			</aside>
		</div>
	</header>

	<CompositionNav />

	<div class="shell start-page">
		<section class="start-section start-guide" aria-labelledby="start-heading">
			<div class="start-heading">
				<p class="eyebrow">Start Here</p>
				<h2 id="start-heading">Choose what you want to read.</h2>
				<p>
					If you are checking the course outcomes, begin with Outcomes & Reflections. Each outcome has my reflection, the artifacts I connect to it, and an explanation of why each artifact belongs there.
				</p>
			</div>

			<nav class="reader-paths" aria-label="Ways to explore the composition portfolio">
				<a class="reader-path reader-path--primary" href="/portfolio/composition/outcomes">
					<span class="reader-path__number">01</span>
					<span class="reader-path__label">Best place to begin</span>
					<strong>Outcomes & Reflections</strong>
					<span class="reader-path__description">Read what I learned for all six outcomes and see the artifacts that support each reflection.</span>
					<span class="reader-path__action">Open reflections <i aria-hidden="true">→</i></span>
				</a>
				<a class="reader-path" href="/portfolio/composition/artifacts">
					<span class="reader-path__number">02</span>
					<span class="reader-path__label">All course work</span>
					<strong>Artifact Index</strong>
					<span class="reader-path__description">Browse all eleven artifacts and see which outcomes connect to each one.</span>
					<span class="reader-path__action">View artifacts <i aria-hidden="true">→</i></span>
				</a>
				<a class="reader-path" href="/portfolio/composition/investigative-field-essay">
					<span class="reader-path__number">03</span>
					<span class="reader-path__label">Completed study</span>
					<strong>Final Research Paper</strong>
					<span class="reader-path__description">Read the interview study, coding table, chart, revision map, and appendix index.</span>
					<span class="reader-path__action">Read the paper <i aria-hidden="true">→</i></span>
				</a>
				<a class="reader-path" href="/portfolio/composition/process-archive">
					<span class="reader-path__number">04</span>
					<span class="reader-path__label">Supporting work</span>
					<strong>Process Archive</strong>
					<span class="reader-path__description">Read the smaller assignments, research-ethics training, reflections, and peer feedback.</span>
					<span class="reader-path__action">Open the archive <i aria-hidden="true">→</i></span>
				</a>
			</nav>
		</section>

		<section class="start-section outcome-map" aria-labelledby="reflection-heading">
			<div class="section-heading section-heading--split">
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow">Outcome Map</p>
					<h2 id="reflection-heading">Find a reflection.</h2>
				</div>
				<p>
					Choose an outcome to go directly to my reflection and the artifacts I use as evidence.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="outcome-map__grid">
				{outcomes.map((outcome) => (
					<a href={`/portfolio/composition/outcomes#${outcome.id}`}>
						<span class="outcome-map__number">{outcome.number}</span>
						<strong>{outcome.title}</strong>
						<span class="outcome-map__count">{outcome.evidence.length} connected artifacts</span>
						<ul aria-label={`Artifacts connected to ${outcome.title}`}>
							{outcome.evidence.map((item) => <li>{item.title}</li>)}
						</ul>
						<i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
					</a>
				))}
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="start-section portfolio-letter" aria-labelledby="letter-heading">
			<div class="section-heading">
				<p class="eyebrow">Cover Letter</p>
				<h2 id="letter-heading">About This Portfolio</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="portfolio-letter__copy">
				<p>
					Before ENC 1102, I mostly saw research as choosing a topic, finding enough sources, and writing a paper. This project made me realize there was more to it than that. I started with something familiar: college students often create unofficial class group chats to ask questions and compare what they think an assignment means. Once I chose that topic, I still had to decide what kind of writing I was studying, find out what earlier research had already covered, and choose a method that would protect the privacy of the people in the chats. I also had to change my claim when the interviews did not fully match what I expected.
				</p>
				<p>
					Almost every major assignment became part of the same project. I set out the question in the Initial Research Proposal, researched four sources for the Annotated Bibliography, and used the CARS exercise to focus on the difference between instructor-managed messaging and student-run chats. I then interviewed five people and coded their answers for recurring ideas. When they brought up incorrect information, notification stress, and students who rarely posted, I changed my original assumption that the chats were mostly helpful. My final argument is that these chats can make it easier to ask questions, restate official instructions in familiar language, and participate by reading or reacting. They can help, but students still need to verify important information and set reasonable boundaries.
				</p>
				<p>
					I separated the portfolio into a start page, an outcomes page, and an artifact index so readers do not have to search one long page for everything. The three major assignments are also available as web pages and downloadable files. The Process Archive contains the smaller assignments, CITI training, and peer feedback I used along the way. The third Gordon Rule artifact is the final paper submitted August 2, while Draft 1 and Revision 1 are still available for comparison.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="start-section major-work" aria-labelledby="major-work-heading">
			<div class="section-heading section-heading--split">
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow">Gordon Rule</p>
					<h2 id="major-work-heading">Three Major Assignments</h2>
				</div>
				<p>These three assignments show the project moving from a question, to source research, to the completed interview study.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="major-work__grid">
				{majorArtifacts.map((artifact) => (
					<article>
						<div class="major-work__meta">
							<span>{artifact.number}</span>
							<span>{artifact.date}</span>
						</div>
						<p>{artifact.type}</p>
						<h3>{artifact.title}</h3>
						<p class="major-work__summary">{artifact.summary}</p>
						<div class="major-work__actions">
							<a href={artifact.href}>Read online <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
							{artifact.download && <a href={artifact.download}>Download <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>}
						</div>
					</article>
				))}
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.composition-hero {
		position: relative;
		overflow: hidden;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
		background:
			linear-gradient(90deg, transparent 0 66%, rgba(193, 165, 126, 0.07) 66% 66.1%, transparent 66.1%),
			radial-gradient(circle at 78% 12%, rgba(92, 126, 100, 0.25), transparent 27rem);
	}

	.composition-hero::after {
		position: absolute;
		top: -200px;
		right: -150px;
		width: 520px;
		height: 520px;
		border: 1px solid rgba(193, 165, 126, 0.18);
		border-radius: 50%;
		content: "";
	}

	.composition-hero__inner {
		position: relative;
		z-index: 1;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(330px, 0.42fr);
		gap: clamp(52px, 8vw, 116px);
		align-items: end;
		min-height: 680px;
		padding-block: clamp(80px, 10vw, 132px);
	}

	.composition-hero h1 {
		max-width: 860px;
		margin: 22px 0 0;
		color: var(--cream);
		font-family: var(--display);
		font-size: clamp(4.2rem, 8.4vw, 8.5rem);
		font-weight: 400;
		letter-spacing: -0.055em;
		line-height: 0.82;
	}

	.composition-hero h1 em {
		color: var(--sage);
		font-weight: 400;
	}

	.composition-hero__deck {
		max-width: 680px;
		margin: 36px 0 0;
		padding-left: 22px;
		border-left: 1px solid var(--tan);
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.5vw, 1.16rem);
		line-height: 1.78;
	}

	.composition-hero__meta {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 10px 24px;
		margin-top: 30px;
		color: var(--sage-bright);
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.09em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.research-card {
		border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
		background: rgba(16, 35, 28, 0.86);
	}

	.research-card__label {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 18px 22px;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
		color: var(--tan);
		font-size: 0.7rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.14em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.research-card__question {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 28px 22px 32px;
		color: var(--cream);
		font-family: var(--display);
		font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 2.8vw, 2.4rem);
		line-height: 1.18;
	}

	.research-card__stats {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.research-card__stats div {
		display: grid;
		gap: 2px;
		padding: 16px 20px;
	}

	.research-card__stats div:nth-child(even) {
		border-left: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.research-card__stats div:nth-child(n + 3) {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.research-card__stats strong {
		color: var(--cream);
		font-family: var(--display);
		font-size: 1.7rem;
		font-weight: 400;
	}

	.research-card__stats span {
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 0.66rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.07em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.start-page {
		padding-block: clamp(64px, 8vw, 108px) 120px;
	}

	.start-section {
		padding-bottom: clamp(78px, 10vw, 126px);
	}

	.start-section + .start-section {
		padding-top: clamp(70px, 8vw, 104px);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
	}

	.start-heading {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(320px, 0.45fr);
		gap: 24px clamp(42px, 7vw, 96px);
		align-items: end;
		margin-bottom: 42px;
	}

	.start-heading .eyebrow {
		grid-column: 1 / -1;
	}

	.start-heading h2,
	.section-heading h2 {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--cream);
		font-family: var(--display);
		font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 6vw, 6rem);
		font-weight: 400;
		letter-spacing: -0.048em;
		line-height: 0.94;
	}

	.start-heading > p:last-child,
	.section-heading > p,
	.section-heading--split > p {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--cream-soft);
		font-size: 0.98rem;
		line-height: 1.8;
	}

	.reader-paths {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 1px;
		border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
		background: var(--rule);
	}

	.reader-path {
		position: relative;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
		gap: 8px 14px;
		min-height: 280px;
		padding: clamp(24px, 4vw, 38px);
		background: var(--paper-soft);
		transition: background-color 180ms ease;
	}

	.reader-path:hover {
		background: var(--paper-raised);
	}

	.reader-path--primary {
		background: var(--forest-deep);
		box-shadow: inset 0 3px 0 var(--tan);
	}

	.reader-path__number {
		color: var(--tan);
		font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
		font-size: 0.72rem;
	}

	.reader-path__label {
		color: var(--sage-bright);
		font-size: 0.68rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.11em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.reader-path strong,
	.outcome-map__grid strong {
		grid-column: 1 / -1;
		color: var(--cream);
		font-family: var(--display);
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.4vw, 3.2rem);
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1;
	}

	.reader-path__description {
		grid-column: 1 / -1;
		max-width: 520px;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 0.88rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.reader-path__action {
		align-self: end;
		grid-column: 1 / -1;
		color: var(--cream-soft);
		font-size: 0.7rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.reader-path__action i {
		margin-left: 8px;
		color: var(--tan);
		font-style: normal;
	}

	.section-heading {
		max-width: 860px;
		margin-bottom: 42px;
	}

	.section-heading .eyebrow {
		margin-bottom: 14px;
	}

	.section-heading--split {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(300px, 0.42fr);
		gap: 32px clamp(44px, 7vw, 96px);
		align-items: end;
		max-width: none;
	}

	.outcome-map__grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 1px;
		border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
		background: var(--rule);
	}

	.outcome-map__grid > a {
		position: relative;
		display: grid;
		align-content: start;
		min-height: 300px;
		padding: 26px;
		background: var(--paper-soft);
		transition: background-color 180ms ease;
	}

	.outcome-map__grid > a:hover {
		background: var(--paper-raised);
	}

	.outcome-map__number {
		margin-bottom: 32px;
		color: var(--tan);
		font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
		font-size: 0.72rem;
	}

	.outcome-map__grid strong {
		font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 2.7vw, 2.6rem);
	}

	.outcome-map__count {
		margin-top: 12px;
		color: var(--sage-bright);
		font-size: 0.66rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.outcome-map__grid ul {
		margin: 18px 0 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}

	.outcome-map__grid li {
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		line-height: 1.45;
	}

	.outcome-map__grid li + li {
		margin-top: 5px;
	}

	.outcome-map__grid i {
		position: absolute;
		top: 24px;
		right: 24px;
		color: var(--tan);
		font-style: normal;
	}

	.portfolio-letter__copy {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 24px clamp(34px, 5vw, 64px);
		max-width: 1060px;
	}

	.portfolio-letter__copy p {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--cream-soft);
		font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.35vw, 1.08rem);
		line-height: 1.9;
	}

	.portfolio-letter__copy p:first-child {
		grid-column: 1 / -1;
		color: var(--sage-bright);
		font-family: var(--display);
		font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.5vw, 2.15rem);
		line-height: 1.34;
	}

	.major-work__grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 1px;
		border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
		background: var(--rule);
	}

	.major-work__grid article {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		min-height: 330px;
		padding: 26px;
		background: var(--paper-soft);
	}

	.major-work__meta {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
		font-size: 0.68rem;
	}

	.major-work__grid article > p:not(.major-work__summary) {
		margin: 34px 0 8px;
		color: var(--tan);
		font-size: 0.64rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.major-work__grid h3 {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--cream);
		font-family: var(--display);
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 3vw, 2.8rem);
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1;
	}

	.major-work__summary {
		margin: 18px 0 26px;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
	}

	.major-work__actions {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 10px 20px;
		margin-top: auto;
	}

	.major-work__actions a {
		color: var(--sage-bright);
		font-size: 0.68rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	@media (max-width: 1000px) {
		.composition-hero__inner {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			min-height: 0;
		}

		.research-card {
			max-width: 620px;
		}

		.outcome-map__grid,
		.major-work__grid {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.composition-hero__inner,
		.start-page {
			width: min(100% - 32px, 1180px);
		}

		.composition-hero__inner {
			padding-block: 64px;
		}

		.composition-hero h1 {
			font-size: clamp(3.4rem, 17vw, 5.2rem);
		}

		.start-heading,
		.section-heading--split,
		.reader-paths,
		.outcome-map__grid,
		.portfolio-letter__copy,
		.major-work__grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}

		.portfolio-letter__copy p:first-child {
			grid-column: auto;
		}

		.reader-path,
		.outcome-map__grid > a,
		.major-work__grid article {
			min-height: 0;
		}

		.reader-path__action {
			margin-top: 24px;
		}
	}
</style>
